---
import Base from '@/layouts/Base.astro';
import ProfileAvatar from '@/components/ProfileAvatar.astro';
import { Separator } from '@/components/ui/separator';
import { SocialLinks } from '@/components/SocialLinks';
---

<Base title="About - Lyes Tarzalt" description="Lyes Tarzalt - Product engineer based in Malaysia, originally from Algeria.">
  <section class="max-w-lg pt-8">
    <ProfileAvatar class="mb-6 size-20 ring-2 ring-primary/20 ring-offset-2 ring-offset-background" />

    <h1 class="font-heading text-3xl font-bold italic tracking-tight">About</h1>

    <div class="mt-8 space-y-5 text-[0.9375rem] leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">
      <p>
        I'm Lyes. Based in <span class="text-foreground">Malaysia</span>, originally from <span class="text-foreground">Algeria</span>.
      </p>
      <p>
        I like building things that help people. When I see a problem, I want to understand why it exists before I start writing code. Most of the time the fix people ask for isn't the fix they need.
      </p>
      <p>
        I run the AI side of things where I work. I sit with clients, learn how their business actually runs, then figure out where an LLM can take boring, repetitive stuff off someone's plate. We once outsourced a voice agent to a third party. The result was slow and the architecture didn't make sense to me, so I couldn't help myself and built a better version on my own time. Our proposal was the last one the client saw, and honestly it wasn't great on paper, but the demo alone got us the deal.
      </p>
      <p>
        Outside of work I make tools I wish existed. <span class="text-foreground">X-Dispatch</span> because X-Plane had no way to browse airports on a map. <span class="text-foreground">Dinar Échange</span> because a friend wanted an easy way to understand currency exchange rates for the Algerian dinar.
      </p>
      <p>
        I think about the whole thing. The architecture, the code, how it looks, how it feels to use. If someone opens the app and has to think about where to click, I messed up.
      </p>
    </div>

    <Separator className="my-10" />

    <h2 class="mb-5 font-heading text-lg font-semibold">Elsewhere</h2>
    <SocialLinks client:load />
  </section>
</Base>
